  "result": "Perfect! All 152 tests pass. Added payment recording functionality to the system.\n\n**New file src/payments.js:**\n\n1. **`recordPayment(invoice, { amount, date })`** \u2014 Records a payment on an invoice\n   - Creates `payments` array if missing\n   - Validates amount is positive integer (cents)\n   - Prevents overpayment (error if payment > balance due)\n   - Status transitions:\n     - `issued` \u2192 `partially_paid` (for partial payment)\n     - `issued` \u2192 `paid` (when fully paid)\n     - `partially_paid` \u2192 `paid` (final payment)\n   - Returns `ok(newInvoice)` or error\n\n2. **`balanceDue(invoice)`** \u2014 Returns amount still owed\n   - Calculates: total - sum of payments\n   - Returns 0 if fully paid\n   - Handles missing/null invoice gracefully\n\n**Error codes added (src/errors.js):**\n- `NOT_ISSUED`: Can only record payments on issued/partially_paid invoices\n- `OVERPAYMENT`: Payment exceeds amount owed\n\n**Tests added (16 payment tests):**\n- \u2713 First payment creates array\n- \u2713 Multiple payments\n- \u2713 Status transitions (issued \u2192 partially_paid \u2192 paid)\n- \u2713 Error validation (amount must be positive integer)\n- \u2713 Overpayment prevention\n- \u2713 Cannot pay on draft or completed invoices\n- \u2713 No input mutation\n- \u2713 Balance due calculations\n- \u2713 Handles edge cases (null, missing data)\n\nKey behavior:\n- Amount is always in cents (integer)\n- No overpayment allowed\n- Status automatically updates based on payment progress\n- Balance due reflects actual amount owed (never negative)\n\nAll 152 tests pass.",
